# [[.Title]]

An [Anetos](https://github.com/anetos-dev/anetos) application[[if .API]]: a JSON
API under `/api/v1`[[else if .Inertia]] whose pages are [[.FrameworkName]] components,
rendered by [Inertia](https://inertiajs.com)'s client[[end]].

```sh
go run . migrate        # create the database tables
go tool anetos dev      # run with live reload on http://localhost:8080[[if .API]]/api/v1[[end]]
go test ./...
```

| Directory | Holds |
|---|---|
| `app/handlers` | HTTP handlers (`go tool anetos make:handler Posts`) |
| `app/models` | Models (`go tool anetos make:model Post --migration`) |
| `app/middleware` | Middleware (`go tool anetos make:middleware Admin`) |
| `database/migrations` | Migrations and seeders (`go tool anetos make:migration create_posts_table`) |
| `database/factories` | Model factories, for tests and seeders |
[[- if .Inertia]]
| `routes` | Routes |
| `frontend` | The pages (`src/pages`), their layout and components, which Vite builds (Node.js); `src/types` is written by `go run . types` |
| `views` | The root view of the pages (`app.templ`), and the emails' |
| `public` | The web root: `robots.txt` and the like, served at `/`, and the frontend's build (`build`) |
| `locales` | The text of the pages and of the server, by locale (`locales/en/app.yaml`), which the pages get in the `messages` prop |
[[- else if .Web]]
| `routes` | Routes |
| `views` | templ components (`go generate ./...` after editing, or `anetos dev`) |
| `public` | The web root: `robots.txt` and the like, served at `/` |
| `public/static` | Static files, served under `/assets` |
[[- else]]
| `routes` | Routes: `api.go`, the API's under `/api/v1` |
| `locales` | The messages' translations (`locales/en/app.yaml`) |
[[- end]]

Configuration is in `.env` (keep it out of git); `.env.example` lists the
settings.

[[- if .Web]]

Add user accounts (registration, login with a password, Google or
GitHub, email verification, password reset, API tokens) with
`go tool anetos make:auth`, then `go run . migrate`.
[[- else]]

Errors are JSON problem details ([RFC 9457](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457)),
whatever the client accepts. Browsers on other origins may call the API
once `HTTP_CORS_ORIGINS` lists them; the app's own SPA logs in with a
session cookie (with make:auth's accounts) once `HTTP_SPA_ORIGINS` lists it.

Add user accounts that log in with API tokens (registration, login
with two-factor codes, email verification, password reset, token
management) with `go tool anetos make:auth`, then `go run . migrate`.
[[- end]]

Add plugins with `go tool anetos add <module>` (and remove them with
`go tool anetos remove <module>`): `plugins.go` lists them, and `main.go`
loads them. See [Use plugins](https://github.com/anetos-dev/anetos/blob/main/docs/site/guides/plugins.md).

Tests use [anetostest](https://github.com/anetos-dev/anetos/blob/main/docs/site/guides/testing.md):
each gets the app with a migrated database, and leaves no rows behind.
[[if eq .DB "sqlite"]]It's an in-memory SQLite database, so there's nothing
to set up.[[else]]`go test` reads the database settings from `.env.testing`,
not `.env`: create the `[[.DBName]]_test` database first.[[end]]

## Deploy

```sh
go tool anetos build    # bin/[[.Bin]]: one binary, everything in it
```

Copy the binary to the server with its settings
(`deploy/production.env.example` lists them) and run `[[.Bin]] migrate`,
then `[[.Bin]] run`; `deploy/[[.Name]].service` does that with systemd.
Or build the image with `docker build -t [[.Image]] .` (the
`Dockerfile`). See [Deploy](https://github.com/anetos-dev/anetos/blob/main/docs/site/guides/deployment.md).
